    "body": "## Summary\n- Make ordinary results quiet and actionable coordination explicit through addressed handoffs, with Kata-first operational guidance.\n- Keep settled history out of hot scans using rebuildable pending-work indexes while retaining canonical recovery/idempotency evidence. Tolerate brief producer contention, honor cancellation, and revalidate authority after locking.\n- Resolve QA execution, published metadata, and delivery/release clearance against one environment authority. Exact-artifact owner reassessments can name a repaired runtime without changing the task, source head, artifact, or historical results.\n\n## Commits\n- `8a38714` Simplify coordination with quiet replies and explicit handoffs\n- `921f835` Index pending coordination work and tolerate producer contention\n- `9958786` Resolve QA environment authority through bounded owner reassessments\n\n## Validation\n- `TMPDIR=/private/tmp flox activate -- go test ./...` passed on the final repair.\n- Focused race checks passed for environment authorization/publication/inheritance, invalid planning-job QA requests, reassessment, and postmerge QA actions; earlier indexing/contention focused race checks also passed.\n- `go vet ./...` and `git diff --check` passed during repair validation.\n- RoboRev1289, 1293, and 1295 passed. Review1294's reachable nil-binding panic was fixed with early QA job/binding validation and a regression test before the final passing review.\n\n## Controlled live validation\nMatching runtime repairs are installed on the master and all four workers. The bounded smoke used one canonical Kata task, one documentation-only PR (#157), and independent Hawk peer review and Wren QA on unchanged head `3d8b82df2fa4e1706953e259189946b307d46074`.\n\n- Repaired-build Rook idle observation: 85.683ms CPU over 60.082255875 seconds (0.142609492% of one core), same PID, no restart.\n- One explicit handoff produced one native turn and one quiet reply with zero downstream deliveries. An idle restart retained byte-identical canonical turn evidence and one reply after 60 seconds.\n- Final Wren review5724018838 approved the bounded smoke against `kata-first-smoke-9958786-v1`; emitted metadata records authenticated handoff `ho_Y5WSN2CDHYQ67VFFQQ3OV5LSIU`. Evidence-body digest and quiet report receipt were verified.\n- Earlier failed observations and QA holds remain preserved. Accepted runtime observations were not replayed simply to obtain a new result. This is bounded smoke evidence, not exhaustive fleet testing or an independent bird engineering review of this runtime diff.\n\nAll worker admissions are held; #157 remains open/unmerged. This PR does not authorize merge, release, or resuming older goals.\n\n## Follow-up boundary\nAutomatic history archival/expiry, a consolidated bounded-rollout command, and clearer admission/status reporting remain follow-up scope.\n",
